    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d604">

                <pb facs="0753" n="661" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg661"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 838.011/34</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Haiti</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bailly-Blanchard</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Port au Prince</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-01-15T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 15, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received January 16, 347
                        a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Minister for Foreign Affairs called today at the Legation and in view of the
                    reported embargo by France on Haitian coffee again brought up the advisability
                    of a declaration of war by Haiti against the Central Powers. He was informed in
                    accordance with Department’s July 3, 4 p.m.,<anchor n="2" xml:id="d604-f1"/>
                    that the matter should be delayed until after <pb facs="0754" n="662"
                        xml:id="pg662"/> the adoption of the constitution conferring powers upon the
                    Council of State.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d604-f2"/> He then inquired when the
                    draft of constitution might be expected and urged earliest opportunity for
                    submission to plebiscite.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Blanchard</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d604-f1" n="2" xml:id="d604-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d604-f2" n="1" xml:id="d604-f2-content">
                <p>By telegram of Jan. 18, the Minister was informed: “Your course of action
                    approved.” (File No. 838.011/34.)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
